        "original_id": "2482156c-03e9-5af2-a2a9-97215ca3adb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, John Indi, Laurens van der Post\n- Films: The Million Dollar Duck, The $1,000,000 Duck, A Far Off Place, The Love Bug, Beethoven, Incident at Victoria Falls, Mandela\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Topics: film adaptations, actor roles, Golden Globe nominations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1971, Walt Disney Productions produced The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, as an American comedy film about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- In 1971, Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- In 1992, Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in Beethoven.\n- In 1992, John Indi appeared in Incident at Victoria Falls.\n- In 1993, A Far Off Place was released as an American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Story Like the Wind (1972) and A Far-Off Place (1974).\n- In 1993, John Indi appeared in A Far Off Place.\n- Dean Jones also played Jim Douglas in The Love Bug in 1968.\n- John Indi is also known for appearing in Mandela.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8d8da385-9c6e-56e7-9cb8-60a045739d92",
        "text": "Page: The Million Dollar Duck. Sentence: The Million Dollar Duck (also titled as The $1,000,000 Duck) is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs scenario.\nPage: A Far Off Place. Sentence: A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works \"A Far-Off Place\" (1974) and its prequel \"A Story Like the Wind\" (1972).\nPage: Dean Jones (actor). Sentence: \" (1965), Jim Douglas in \"The Love Bug\" (1968), Albert Dooley in \"The Million Dollar Duck\" (1971; for which he received a Golden Globe nomination) and Dr. Herman Varnick in \"Beethoven\" (1992).\nPage: John Indi. Sentence: John Indi is an actor known for his roles in \"A Far Off Place\" (1993), \"Mandela\", and \"Incident at Victoria Falls\" (1992).",
